Subject: Reduce-Chunk-Tick-Overhead

Author: VeltisMC Development Team
Date: 2026-06-19

Reason:
Vanilla chunk ticking iterates all loaded chunks sequentially, applying
random ticks, block entity ticks, and entity ticks without prioritizing
chunks near players. This wastes CPU on chunks far from any player and
creates uneven tick distribution.

Impact:
More consistent tick times. Reduced CPU usage from ticking irrelevant
chunks. Better TPS stability on servers with large worlds.

Migration Note:
This patch enables Moonrise's chunk tick iteration system, which
groups chunks by distance to players and allocates tick time
proportionally. The tick loop also handles catch-up ticks
configurably via moonrise.yml tick-loop.catchup-ticks.
